  "description": "CreateDatabase(path, dbLangGeneral, dbVersion120). KA(k primary key: keys 3, 1, 2; t 'a1' to 'a3') and KB(k no index: keys 2, 1, 3, 1; u 'b1' to 'b4') as in r-q5-join-order/inner-index, where the snapshot drives KB in storage order and probes KA. Each of SELECT t, u FROM KA INNER JOIN KB ON KA.k = KB.k; SELECT t, u FROM KB INNER JOIN KA ON KA.k = KB.k; SELECT t, u FROM KA LEFT JOIN KB ON KA.k = KB.k; SELECT t, u FROM KB LEFT JOIN KA ON KA.k = KB.k opened as a dynaset and then as a snapshot, all rows read. Asks whether a join's dynaset comes in its snapshot's order or in another (a key order of either table).",
